      "message": "\u003e I think its already covered by \u0027import \u0027? I tried a long line with import type and no warnings were seen.\n\nAck.\n\n\u003e Using export { and export type { here is to avoid generating warnings for examples like export const LONGLONGLONGLONGLONGSTRING \u003d veryverylonglonglonglonglonglongstring\n\nI see. This seems quite incomplete though, as a long string can appear anywhere like `console.log(\u0027superlongstring.....\u0027)` and same for a long constant/var name without the use of `export`. Perhaps `export type` is better removed from here given on how incomplete this suppression would be, but don\u0027t have a strong opinion.",
