      "writtenOn": "2026-01-23T01:25:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oops sorry, didn\u0027t realize there was a mistake in my wording.\nWe want to suppress the presubmit length warnings for the following cases because they will not be auto-formatted by `git cl format`:\n- export {somehandler} from \u0027longlonglonglonglonglonglonglongpath.js\u0027\n- export type {SomeType} from \u0027longlonglonglonglonglonglonglongpath.js\u0027. \n\nFor other export use cases, we don\u0027t skip the length check as they will be auto-formatted by `git cl format`. For example:\n- export class someElement extends someElementBase {}\n- export const superlonglonglongstring \u003d \u0027longlonglonglong\u0027\n\nTL;DR: Have the presubmit check aligned with clang-format, but I agree the suppression here is limited.",
